    "about": {
      "title": "About Me",
      "body": "<p><span class=\"key-term\">A bit of everything.</span> As an <span class=\"key-term\">urban artist</span> and <span class=\"key-term\">multimedia designer</span>, I always look for <span class=\"key-term\">new tools</span> to push my creative process. From <span class=\"key-term\">graffiti to design</span>, I sought projects that connected these two worlds: street art and tech, exploring future relationships between people and urban spaces.</p><p><span class=\"key-term\">This research took a new direction when I was selected for the Apple Developer Academy</span>, Apple's international program focused on innovation, <span class=\"key-term\">user-centered design, and software development through real-world challenges and multidisciplinary collaboration</span>. During this period, I deepened my practice in <span class=\"key-term\">extended reality</span> and <span class=\"key-term\">spatial computing</span>, while exploring <span class=\"key-term\">Web 3.0 and emerging futures</span>.</p><p><span class=\"key-term\">From there, I found myself naturally drawn to this field</span>, which led me to work on the <span class=\"key-term\">curation and development of augmented reality exhibitions</span> across <span class=\"key-term\">Brazil</span>, including an exhibition at the <span class=\"key-term\">Embassy of Mexico</span> in Brasília honoring Frida Kahlo.</p><p><span class=\"key-term\">This background became part of my work as a New Media Designer at creative studio DELED.</span> Bringing this experience into larger-scale projects, I contributed to projects for <span class=\"key-term\">Museu do Amanhã</span>, <span class=\"key-term\">Rock in Rio</span>, and other major brands and institutions, developing <span class=\"key-term\">interactive and immersive experiences</span> connecting art and tech.</p>"
    },
